  "question": {
    "text": "A student needs to prepare a buffer solution of propanoic acid and its sodium salt with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi><mn>4</mn></math>. The ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>COO</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></mrow></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>COOH</mi></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math> required to make buffer is Given :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>COOH</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></math>"
  },
